• laws and policies of the U.S. and other jurisdictions affecting trade, foreign investment, loans, and taxes; and
• geopolitical events, including war and terrorism.
As international physical, e-commerce, and omnichannel retail and other services grow, competition will intensify, including
through adoption of evolving business models. Local companies may have a substantial competitive advantage because of their greater
understanding of, and focus on, the local customer, as well as their more established local brand names.

